                <pb facs="0291" n="171" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg171"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">816.00 Revolutions/5: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in El Salvador</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Curtis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San Salvador</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-12-03T09:00:00-06:00">December 3, 1931—9 a.m. [<hi
                                rendition="#italic">p.m.</hi>]</date><lb/>[Received 11:26
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>102. My 101, December 3, 7 p.m. President reached Santa Ana at 7:30 and the Army
                    Commander gave him command of the town. I believe nevertheless his chances are
                    hopeless.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Curtis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
